 x=\"3\" y=\"4\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18\"/></svg></span><span><b>Up to 1 year</b>of access, or until you pass</span></li></ul>"}, "elements": []}]}]}, {"id": "63aff88", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "boxed", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "40", "row": "40", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 40}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "104", "right": "64", "bottom": "104", "left": "64", "isLinked": false}, "boxed_width": {"unit": "px", "size": 1312, "sizes": []}, "flex_gap_mobile": {"column": "28", "row": "28", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 28}, "padding_tablet": {"unit": "px", "top": "80", "right": "40", "bottom": "80", "left": "40", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "64", "right": "20", "bottom": "64", "left": "20", "isLinked": false}, "html_tag": "section"}, "elements": [{"id": "05634b2", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "64", "row": "64", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 64}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": false}, "flex_gap_tablet": {"column": "40", "row": "40", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 40}, "flex_gap_mobile": {"column": "32", "row": "32", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 32}, "css_classes": "g-twocol"}, "elements": [{"id": "bd89b38", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "40", "row": "40", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 40}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": false}, "flex_gap_mobile": {"column": "32", "row": "32", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 32}, "css_classes": "g-main"}, "elements": [{"id": "c61655f", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 16}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "3c04360", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "isInner": false, "settings": {"title": "Why you should buy this class", "header_size": "h2", "__globals__": {"title_color": "globals/colors?id=navy", "typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=h2"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "f5c5266", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "isInner": false, "settings": {"editor": "<p>A Board rule from 2005 requires you to submit this Residential Design Class Certificate of Completion with your Conditioned Air license application. The License Board will not process your application without it.</p><p>The certificate is required to apply for the Restricted (Class 1) license or the Non-Restricted (Class 2) license.</p>", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=body", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=ink"}, "_css_classes": "g-prose "}, "elements": []}]}, {"id": "b668296", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 16}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "9e6d814", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "isInner": false, "settings": {"title": "What it covers", "header_size": "h2", "__globals__": {"title_color": "globals/colors?id=navy", "typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=h2"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e24a83e", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "isInner": false, "settings": {"editor": "<p>The Certificate of Completion requires 16 hours of class time, covering the ACCA design manuals J and D.</p><ul class=\"g-list\"><li><b>ACCA Manual J:</b> residential heat loss/gain load calculation</li><li><b>ACCA Manual D:</b> residential duct design calculation</li></ul><p>This class is very important for passing the exam. When people fail, it is almost always in the design category, mostly Manual D (duct design).</p>", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=body", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=ink"}, "_css_classes": "g-prose "}, "elements": []}]}, {"id": "8e9efa1", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 16}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "27e5bd4", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "isInner": false, "settings": {"title": "How the class works", "header_size": "h2", "__globals__": {"title_color": "globals/colors?id=navy", "typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=h2"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "7708580", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "isInner": false, "settings": {"editor": "<ul class=\"g-list\"><li>I do not give the answers, I give you the solutions. The videos show every step I take to solve the equations.</li><li>A GLEC Residential Design Study Guide is included, with exam-type questions from each design book and full solutions, so you can follow how each equation is solved.</li><li>Class length is about 16 hours of video. Add 4 to 6 hours online to highlight the books, and about 8 to 12 more hours for the calculations.</li><li>Print your Certificate of Completion online after watching all the videos. Print 3 copies and save one as a PDF for your application.</li><li>This class has been online since April 2018. We have sold 1,740 online classes through October 2026, with an exam pass rate of about 82%.</li></ul>", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=body", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=ink"}, "_css_classes": "g-prose "}, "elements": []}]}, {"id": "f870111", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 16}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": false}}, "elements": [{"id": "ca3f38d", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "isInner": false, "settings": {"title": "Before you apply", "header_size": "h2", "__globals__": {"title_color": "globals/colors?id=navy", "typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=h2"}}, "elements": []}, {"id": "2392973", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "isInner": false, "settings": {"editor": "<ul class=\"g-list\"><li>EPA-608 technician certification, Type 2 or higher, is required in your application package. <a href=\"https://staging158.dreamweb.digital/technician-certifications/\">See technician certifications</a>.</li><li>You are responsible for buying the required Reference Books for the classes you purchase. <a href=\"https://sebookstore.com/glec.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Order the Reference Books</a>.</li><li>This Certificate of Completion can also be used for NATE CEHs. Submit a copy to NATE at your renewal.</li></ul>", "__globals__": {"typography_typography": "globals/typography?id=body", "text_color": "globals/colors?id=ink"}, "_css_classes": "g-prose "}, "elements": []}]}, {"id": "fa1b6d2", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "html", "isInner": false, "settings": {"html": "<details class=\"g-more\"><summary>See More <span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div class=\"g-more__body\"><p>This class is also known as &ldquo;The Residential Heat Loss/Gain &amp; Duct Design Class&rdquo;.</p><p>Board Rule from the year 2005 requires you to submit this Residential Design Class Certificate of Completion with your &ldquo;CA&rdquo; Conditioned Air License Application. The License Board will NOT process your Application without it!</p><p>This Certificate of Completion is required to APPLY for the Restricted (Class 1) License or the Non-Restricted (Class 2) License applicants.</p><p>Certificate of Completion requires 16 hours of class time, covering ACCA Design Manuals J and D.</p><ul><li>ACCA Manual J = Residential Heat Loss/Gain Load Calculation</li><li>ACCA Manual D = Residential Duct Design Calculation</li></ul><p>EPA-608 Technician Certification of Type 2 or Higher is Required to be in your Application submittal package. If you need to get this, go to <a href=\"/technician-certifications/\">Technician Certifications</a>.</p><p>A GLEC Residential Design Study Guide is included with Exam type questions from each design book, with solutions (not just the answers) so you can follow in solving the equation or solution.</p><p>You are responsible for Purchasing all the required Reference Books for the classes you purchased. Go to Quick Links to find the Reference Book list, and to also Purchase Order the Books.</p><p>This Residential Design class is very important in passing the Exam to get your License. When people fail, it is almost always in the &ldquo;Design&rdquo; category, mostly Manual D (Duct Design).</p><p>Note: this Certificate of Completion can be used for NATE CEH&rsquo;s. You would have to submit a copy of your Certificate of Completion to NATE at your Renewal.</p><p>Class length is about 16 hours of Videos, add 4&ndash;6 hours Online to Highlight the Books. Add about 8&ndash;12 more hours for doing the calculations.</p><p>You would Print your Certificate of Completion Online, after watching all the videos. Print 3 copies and one as a PDF for your Application.</p><h3>More Class Details</h3><ol><li>Available On-Demand 24/7 As many times, through your Exam, up to one year after your date of purchase of the class, or until you pass your Exam, whichever comes first. Can be extended if needed, for a fair fee, based on length of time from purchase date.</li><li>I do not give the answers, I give you the SOLUTIONS. The Videos show every little step I take to solve the equations.</li><li>This class has been Online since April 2018.</li><li>We have sold 1740 Online classes through October 2026.</li><li>Exam passing rate has been more successful, about 82%.</li></ol></div></details>"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "089d48e", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "html", "isInner": false, "settings": {"html": "<div class=\"g-callout g-callout--info\"><span class=\"g-callout__ico\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4M12 8h.01\"/></svg></span><div><p class=\"g-callout__t\">Access</p><p>Available on demand, 24/7, as many times as you like: up to one year after the date you buy the class, or until you pass your exam, whichever comes first. Access can be extended if needed for a fair fee, based on how long it has been since you bought it.</p></div></div>"}, "elements": []}]}, {"id": "c14169e", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "0", "row": "0", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 0}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": false}, "css_classes": "g-aside"}, "elements": [{"id": "8b87d59", "elType": "container", "isInner": false, "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "flex_gap": {"column": "16", "row": "16", "isLinked": true, "unit": "px", "size": 16}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "28", "right": "28", "bottom": "28", "left": "28", "isLinked": false}, "padding_mobile": {"unit": "px", "top": "22", "right": "20", "bottom": "22", "left": "20", "isLinked": false}, "css_classes": "g-buy"}, "elements": [{"id": "28f903b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "html", "isInner": fals